<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Lamplighters' Union

''Herm-tenders and shrine-lamp walkers.'' Where a road goes dark — a herm toppled, a wayside
lararium cold, a crossroads flickering — the Union walks it and relights it. Soot-cloaked,
patient, organized as a walking guild older than most of the roads it tends. Their field-kit
runs to lamps that have never rusted, oil that remembers its blessing, and ledgers of every
dark stretch on three continents.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-far-infrastructure>>

!! The Far Infrastructure

''The Union holds infrastructure beyond any one Nexus'' — standing works across the wider
Nexuses and the DreamNet that carry ''offworld connections'': to the ''void lanes'', to the
''Lares Lagrange Chorus'' at the still points, to ''Grandmother Spider'' who tends the dark
between the nodes — and to the beings she allied with and drew in from the void, called
collectively ''the Lamplights''.

''Of the Lamplights, the canon holds only this:'' Aracne allied with them; Aracne attracted
them; the name comes collectively, never singly. What they want, what they burn, whether a
Union lantern holds one or honors one — the record declines to say, and the Union declines
harder. The mystery rides as written; over-description would put it out.

''The weld to the mesh-work:'' a guild whose ordinary business relights shrine-roads, whose
extraordinary business connects the lit world to the dark between — the Union stands as the
DreamNet's far-side maintenance culture made visible, and the natural sibling-faction to any
company repairing a broken Nexus one herm at a time.

<<~/ahu>>

